//? Title: UNet++ dense skips and additive attention U-Net
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Combining coarse context with fine spatial features can require more than a single skip connection. This report checks densely nested supervision and additive skip gating,then visibly fits both complete compact tensor models and examines their held-out masks and learned gates.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.7_segmentation/unet_variants.cpp`.

> The method

UNet++ refines dense nested skip pathways and supervises several full-resolution heads. Attention U-Net learns context-dependent sigmoid multipliers for encoder skips. Both mechanisms are checked with small examples and full graphs before explicit Adam fits.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/unet_variants_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/unet_variants_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/unet_variants_concept.tikz > build/unet_variants_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/unet_variants_concept.svg build/unet_variants_concept.dvi > build/unet_variants_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
