> Dense nested skips and complete model graphs

UNet++ constructs x[i,j] by concatenating all earlier x[i,0..j-1] nodes with
corner-aligned bilinear upsampling of x[i+1,j-1] to the actual encoder shape,
then applying two3x3/ReLU convolutions. Four full-resolution learned heads
provide deep supervision; evaluation uses the deepest head. At default base32,
the deepest x[0,4] concatenates192 channels and the graph has15 nodes,
9,156,264 learned scalars and68 learned tensor gradients.

Attention U-Net uses learned2x2 stride2 up-convolutions,one additive gate for
each cropped encoder skip,and concatenated decoder convolution pairs.
At default base64,it has31,381,414 scalars and70 tensor gradients. The
adaptation omits BN and dropout in both models. Full graphs execute below at
32x32 with initialized weights,without a biomedical accuracy claim. Compact
base8/four-class models retain every nested node/head or every attention gate.
Native checks require every compact gradient to be nonzero and verify dense
concatenation widths,odd nested alignment and rounded attention geometry.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (bool nested : {true, false}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(17);
    const auto x = n::sin(.13 * n::arange(0, 32 * 32 * 3)).reshape({1, 32, 32, 3});
    n::Tensor loss;
    std::size_t heads = 1, nodes = 0;
    if (nested) {
      const auto net = m::NestedUnet(p, x);
      heads = net.heads.size();
      nodes = net.nodes.size();
      loss = n::mean(n::square(net.heads[0]));
      for (std::size_t i = 1; i < heads; ++i)
        loss = loss + n::mean(n::square(net.heads[i]));
      if (p.at("x0_4/conv1/W").shape()[2] != 192 || heads != 4 || nodes != 15)
        return 1;
    } else {
      const auto net = m::AttentionUnet(p, x);
      loss = n::mean(n::square(net.logits));
      if (net.coefficients.size() != 4)
        return 1;
    }
    const auto g = n::grad(loss, p.parameters());
    if (p.count() != (nested ? 9156264 : 31381414) || g.size() != (nested ? 68 : 70))
      return 1;
    for (const auto &v : g)
      if (!v.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::sum(n::square(v.to(n::DType::Float64))).item()))
        return 1;
    std::print("Full{}:{} learned scalars,all{} finite defined gradients at32px,{} supervised "
               "heads,{} nested nodes,no BN state.\n",
               nested ? "UNet++" : "attention U-Net", p.count(), g.size(), heads, nodes);
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
FullUNet++:9156264 learned scalars,all68 finite defined gradients at32px,4 supervised heads,15 nested nodes,no BN state.
Fullattention U-Net:31381414 learned scalars,all70 finite defined gradients at32px,1 supervised heads,0 nested nodes,no BN state.
// result_end

> Actual shape images and visible deep-supervised Adam fitting

The tensor generator supplies32 fitting/16 validation/16 test48-pixel RGB
shape scenes,seeds11/22/33,with class-independent brightness/noise/tint and
occlusion. Tensor RNG changes the old mt19937 fixed-seed pixels; this is the
same explicit procedural adaptation as the other segmentation reports.
Palette: background dark,circle red,rectangle green,triangle blue.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/unet_variants_data.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto data = m::TensorSegmentationShapes(32, 48, 11);
  std::vector<n::Tensor> gallery;
  const auto colored = m::ColorSegmentationLabels(n::slice_axis(data.labels, 0, 0, 4));
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(data.images, 0, i, i + 1));
    gallery.push_back(n::slice_axis(colored, 0, i, i + 1));
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat(gallery, 0), "build/unet_variants_data.png", 2, 0., 1., 3, 1.,
                     2);
  const auto weights = m::SegmentationClassWeights(data.labels, 4);
  std::print(
      "32 fitting RGB images48x48; classes0 background,1 circle,2 rectangle,3 triangle. "
      "Fit-only inverse-square-root pseudocount weights {:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}/{:.6f}. "
      "Noise,tint and brightness are class-independent; later objects occlude earlier masks. "
      "Tensor RNG changes fixed-seed pixels relative to the old mt19937 generator.\n",
      weights.at({0}), weights.at({1}), weights.at({2}), weights.at({3}));
}
```
